  "summary": "< MISSIONARY WORK >\nFounded a non-profit organization called INTERNATIONAL LIVINGWAY MISSION.\n\n\n< COMPUTER PROGRAMING PROJECTS >\n\nKEY PROJECTS\n\nWeb-Based Projects & Mobile Apps:\nCurrently I am developing B2B and B2C projects in .NET MVC and Mobile App in .NET MAUI.\n\nPOS (Point-of-Sale) Software:\nCreated POS software from the scratch with a team in C#, .NET Framework and MSSQL.  Integrated peripherals to the software.\n\nCredit Card Payment Module (PayPlus):\nCreated a credit card payment module (PayPlus) according to PCI regulations, and received PA-DSS certified by PCI-DSS.  It receives transactions from local POS system, and send them to a processor.  Then, it returns the results of processing from the processor to the POS system.\n\nPayPlus Solutions Project & Demo Program:\nThis application verifies the credentials of the PayPlus.  So, PayPlus module cannot be used without PayPlus Solutions application.  Demo program is to demonstrate how to use PayPlus module.\n\nSoftware Activation Program, API for Software Product Key, and Management Site:\nCreated APIs to create product keys, to do and check activations, and to manage keys and activations of software.  Made in WCF Soap Service.  The Activation Program is an independent software, which means it can be used by any other software.  Management Site creates product keys, and can activate software manually when there is an internet connection problem.  Also can reset or deactivate software.\n\nAPI for Reward System, Demo Program, and Management Site:\nCreated APIs for Reward System Project in WCF Rest Service.  Enhanced security using OAuth 2.0, which is the industry-standard protocol for authorization.  Has credit card processing, Has a feature of earning/redeeming rewards points and stamps.  The Demo Program is to demonstrate how to use the APIs.\n\nDatabase Synchronization:\nDeveloped a sync program to synchronize database between local POS and CLOUD.\n\nDatabase Architecture:\nDesigned and created database for various projects.  Created Stored Procedures, Views, Functions, and Triggers.  I have MCDBA certification, and been using MSSQL since version 6.5.",
